        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What exactly is the AWPR and is it the same road as the A90 or A96?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>The AWPR, also known as the Aberdeen Western Peripheral Route, is the bypass built around the west of Aberdeen to take through-traffic away from the city centre. Sections of it are signed as part of the A90 and A96, since it links the north and south A90 with the A96 towards Inverurie. If you're not sure which stretch you're on, the nearest junction number or a landmark such as Craibstone, Kingswells or Charleston is more useful to us than the road name.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Are there fewer places to pull over on the AWPR than on other roads into Aberdeen?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Yes, broadly. As a newer bypass built for free-flowing traffic, the AWPR has long open sections between junctions with limited laybys, so a suitable stopping point can be further away than on some older roads. If your vehicle is showing signs of trouble, try to reach the next slip road or junction while it's still safe to keep driving, rather than waiting until you're forced to stop on the main carriageway.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do you cover the AWPR near Westhill and Kingswells as well as further round towards Balmedie?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Yes, we cover the AWPR along its route around the west of Aberdeen, including the Westhill and Kingswells sections and the Dyce and Craibstone stretch towards the A96. Give us your nearest junction and direction of travel when you call.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

